nimize token overhead.\nFILE /root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/automation/cron-vs-heartbeat.md:278:- Batch similar checks into heartbeat instead of multiple cron jobs.\nFILE /root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/automation/cron-vs-heartbeat.md:279:- Use `target: \"none\"` on heartbeat if you only want internal processing.\nFILE /root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/automation/cron-vs-heartbeat.md:280:- Use isolated cron with a cheaper model for routine tasks.\nFILE /root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/automation/cron-vs-heartbeat.md:284:- [Heartbeat](/gateway/heartbeat) - full heartbeat configuration\nFILE /root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/automation/cron-vs-heartbeat.md:285:- [Cron jobs](/automation/cron-jobs) - full cron CLI and API reference\nFILE /root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/automation/cron-vs-heartbeat.md:286:- [System](/cli/system) - system events + heartbeat controls\nFILE /root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/automation/cron-jobs.md:2:summary: \"Cron jobs + wakeups for the Gateway scheduler\"\nFILE /root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/automation/cron-jobs.md:5:  - Wiring automation that should run with or alongside heartbeats\nFILE /root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/automation/cron-jobs.md:6:  - Deciding between heartbeat and cron for scheduled tasks\nFILE /root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/automation/cron-jobs.md:7:title: \"Cron Jobs\"\nFILE /root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/automation/cron-jobs.md:10:# Cron jobs (Gateway scheduler)\nFILE /root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/automation/cron-jobs.md:12:> **Cron vs Heartbeat?** See [Cron vs Heartbeat](/automation/cron-vs-heartbeat) for guidance on when to use each.\nFILE /root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/automation/cron-jobs.md:14:Cron is the Gateway’s built-in scheduler. It persists jobs, wakes the agent at\nFILE /root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/automation/cron-jobs.md:18:cron is the mechanism.\nFILE /root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/automation/cron-jobs.md:24:- Cron runs **inside the Gateway** (not inside the model).\nFILE /root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/automation/cron-jobs.md:25:- Jobs persist under `~/.openclaw/cron/` so restarts don’t lose schedules.\nFILE /root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/automation/cron-jobs.md:27:  - **Main session**: enqueue a system event, then run on the next heartbeat.\nFILE /root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/automation/cron-jobs.md:28:  - **Isolated**: run a dedicated agent turn in `cron:<jobId>`, with delivery (announce by default or none).\nFILE /root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/automation/cron-jobs.md:29:- Wakeups are first-class: a job can request “wake now” vs “next heartbeat”.\nFILE /root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/automation/cron-jobs.md:31:- Legacy fallback remains for stored jobs with `notify: true` when `cron.webhook` is set, migrate those jobs to webhook delivery mode.\nFILE /root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/automation/cron-jobs.md:38:openclaw cron add \\\nFILE /root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/automation/cron-jobs.md:42:  --system-event \"Reminder: check the cron docs draft\" \\\nFILE /root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/automation/cron-jobs.md:46:openclaw cron list\nFILE /root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/automation/cron-jobs.md:47:openclaw cron run <job-id>\nFILE /root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/automation/cron-jobs.md:48:openclaw cron runs --id <job-id>\nFILE /root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/automation/cron-jobs.md:54:openclaw cron add \\\nFILE /root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/automation/cron-jobs.md:56:  --cron \"0 7 * * *\" \\\nFILE /root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/automation/cron-jobs.md:65:## Tool-call equivalents (Gateway cron tool)\nFILE /root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/automation/cron-jobs.md:67:For the canonical JSON shapes and examples, see [JSON schema for tool calls](/automation/cron-jobs#json-schema-for-tool-calls).\nFILE /root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/automation/cron-jobs.md:69:## Where cron jobs are stored\nFILE /root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/automation/cron-jobs.md:71:Cron jobs are persisted on the Gateway host at `~/.openclaw/cron/jobs.json` by default.\nFILE /root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/automation/cron-jobs.md:73:are only safe when the Gateway is stopped. Prefer `openclaw cron add/edit` or the cron\nFILE /root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/automation/cron-jobs.md:78:Think of a cron job as: **when** to run + **what** to do.\nFILE /root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/automation/cron-jobs.md:82:   - Repeating job → `schedule.kind = \"every\"` or `schedule.kind = \"cron\"`\nFILE /root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/automation/cron-jobs.md:86:   - `sessionTarget: \"main\"` → run during the next heartbeat with main context.\nFILE /root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/automation/cron-jobs.md:87:   - `sessionTarget: \"isolated\"` → run a dedicated agent turn in `cron:<jobId>`.\nFILE /root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/automation/cron-jobs.md:100:A cron job is a stored record with:\nFILE /root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/automation/cron-jobs.md:114:Cron supports three schedule kinds:\nFILE /root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/automation/cron-jobs.md:118:- `cron`: 5-field cron expression (or 6-field with seconds) with optional IANA timezone.\nFILE /root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/automation/cron-jobs.md:120:Cron expressions use `croner`. If a timezone is omitted, the Gateway host’s\nFILE /root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/automation/cron-jobs.md:128:For any cron schedule, you can set an explicit stagger window with `schedule.staggerMs`\nFILE /root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/automation/cron-jobs.md:138:Main jobs enqueue a system event and optionally wake the heartbeat runner.\nFILE /root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/automation/cron-jobs.md:141:- `wakeMode: \"now\"` (default): event triggers an immediate heartbeat run.\nFILE /root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/automation/cron-jobs.md:142:- `wakeMode: \"next-heartbeat\"`: event waits for the next scheduled heartbeat.\nFILE /root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/automation/cron-jobs.md:144:This is the best fit when you want the normal heartbeat prompt + main-session context.\nFILE /root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/automation/cron-jobs.md:145:See [Heartbeat](/gateway/heartbeat).\nFILE /root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/automation/cron-jobs.md:147:#### Isolated jobs (dedicated cron sessions)\nFILE /root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/automation/cron-jobs.md:149:Isolated jobs run a dedicated agent turn in session `cron:<jobId>`.\nFILE /root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/automation/cron-jobs.md:153:- Prompt is prefixed with `[cron:<jobId> <job name>]` for traceability.\nFILE /root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/automation/cron-jobs.md:161:  - `now`: immediate heartbeat.\nFILE /root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/automation/cron-jobs.md:162:  - `next-heartbeat`: waits for the next scheduled heartbeat.\nFILE /root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/automation/cron-jobs.md:171:- `systemEvent`: main-session only, routed through the heartbeat prompt.\nFILE /root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/automation/cron-jobs.md:177:- `model` / `thinking`: optional overrides (see below).\nFILE /root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/automation/cron-jobs.md:195:When `delivery.mode = \"announce\"`, cron delivers directly via the outbound channel adapters.\nFILE /root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/automation/cron-jobs.md:202:- Heartbeat-only responses (`HEARTBEAT_OK` with no real content) are not delivered.\nFILE /root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/automation/cron-jobs.md:207:- The main-session summary respects `wakeMode`: `now` triggers an immediate heartbeat and\nFILE /root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/automation/cron-jobs.md:208:  `next-heartbeat` waits for the next scheduled heartbeat.\nFILE /root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/automation/cron-jobs.md:212:When `delivery.mode = \"webhook\"`, cron posts the finished event payload to `delivery.to` when the finished event includes a summary.\nFILE /root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/automation/cron-jobs.md:219:- If `cron.webhookToken` is set, auth header is `Authorization: Bearer <cron.webhookToken>`.\nFILE /root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/automation/cron-jobs.md:220:- Deprecated fallback: stored legacy jobs with `notify: true` still post to `cron.webhook` (if configured), with a warning so you can migrate to `delivery.mode = \"webhook\"`.\nFILE /root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6