9A1mlzBXcx11z9eUrIcsAGpQv0=\",\"summary\":[{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Exploring skill execution**\\n\\nI’m thinking I need to find out about the current execution of the find-skills skill since the user has mentioned it specifically. It makes sense to check the mandatory skills involved, and maybe I should dive into how find-skills works exactly. By reading the SKILL.md file, I can understand precisely how this skill operates and ensure I’m giving accurate information based on the user’s needs. Let’s see what I find!\"}]}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_UIJCAmhBvNs9tR3p4WByBFlJ|fc_06eb29bac2029a2b0169b5713a80648191aa43284450a947ae","name":"read","arguments":{"file_path":"/root/.openclaw/workspace/skills/find-skills/SKILL.md"},"partialJson":"{\"file_path\":\"/root/.openclaw/workspace/skills/find-skills/SKILL.md\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":805,"output":99,"cacheRead":158464,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":159368,"cost":{"input":0.0020125,"output":0.001485,"cacheRead":0.039616,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0431135}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1773498675611}}
{"type":"message","id":"3ddec455","parentId":"e7d15afe","timestamp":"2026-03-14T14:31:22.872Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_UIJCAmhBvNs9tR3p4WByBFlJ|fc_06eb29bac2029a2b0169b5713a80648191aa43284450a947ae","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"---\nname: find-skills\ndescription: Helps users discover and install agent skills when they ask questions like \"how do I do X\", \"find a skill for X\", \"is there a skill that can...\", or express interest in extending capabilities. This skill should be used when the user is looking for functionality that might exist as an installable skill.\n---\n\n# Find Skills\n\nThis skill helps you discover and install skills from the open agent skills ecosystem.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\nUse this skill when the user:\n\n- Asks \"how do I do X\" where X might be a common task with an existing skill\n- Says \"find a skill for X\" or \"is there a skill for X\"\n- Asks \"can you do X\" where X is a specialized capability\n- Expresses interest in extending agent capabilities\n- Wants to search for tools, templates, or workflows\n- Mentions they wish they had help with a specific domain (design, testing, deployment, etc.)\n\n## What is the Skills CLI?\n\nThe Skills CLI (`npx skills`) is the package manager for the open agent skills ecosystem. Skills are modular packages that extend agent capabilities with specialized knowledge, workflows, and tools.\n\n**Key commands:**\n\n- `npx skills find [query]` - Search for skills interactively or by keyword\n- `npx skills add <package>` - Install a skill from GitHub or other sources\n- `npx skills check` - Check for skill updates\n- `npx skills update` - Update all installed skills\n\n**Browse skills at:** https://skills.sh/\n\n## How to Help Users Find Skills\n\n### Step 1: Understand What They Need\n\nWhen a user asks for help with something, identify:\n\n1. The domain (e.g., React, testing, design, deployment)\n2. The specific task (e.g., writing tests, creating animations, reviewing PRs)\n3. Whether this is a common enough task that a skill likely exists\n\n### Step 2: Search for Skills\n\nRun the find command with a relevant query:\n\n```bash\nnpx skills find [query]\n```\n\nFor example:\n\n- User asks \"how do I make my React app faster?\" → `npx skills find react performance`\n- User asks \"can you help me with PR reviews?\" → `npx skills find pr review`\n- User asks \"I need to create a changelog\" → `npx skills find changelog`\n\nThe command will return results like:\n\n```\nInstall with npx skills add <owner/repo@skill>\n\nvercel-labs/agent-skills@vercel-react-best-practices\n└ https://skills.sh/vercel-labs/agent-skills/vercel-react-best-practices\n```\n\n### Step 3: Present Options to the User\n\nWhen you find relevant skills, present them to the user with:\n\n1. The skill name and what it does\n2. The install command they can run\n3. A link to learn more at skills.sh\n\nExample response:\n\n```\nI found a skill that might help! The \"vercel-react-best-practices\" skill provides\nReact and Next.js performance optimization guidelines from Vercel Engineering.\n\nTo install it:\nnpx skills add vercel-labs/agent-skills@vercel-react-best-practices\n\nLearn more: https://skills.sh/vercel-labs/agent-skills/vercel-react-best-practices\n```\n\n### Step 4: Offer to Install\n\nIf the user wants to proceed, you can install the skill for them:\n\n```bash\nnpx skills add <owner/repo@skill> -g -y\n```\n\nThe `-g` flag installs globally (user-level) and `-y` skips confirmation prompts.\n\n## Common Skill Categories\n\nWhen searching, consider these common categories:\n\n| Category        | Example Queries                          |\n| --------------- | ---------------------------------------- |\n| Web Development | react, nextjs, typescript, css, tailwind |\n| Testing         | testing, jest, playwright, e2e           |\n| DevOps          | deploy, docker, kubernetes, ci-cd        |\n| Documentation   | docs, readme, changelog, api-docs        |\n| Code Quality    | review, lint, refactor, best-practices   |\n| Design          | ui, ux, design-system, accessibility     |\n| Productivity    | workflow, automation, git                |\n\n## Tips for Effective Searches\n\n1. **Use specific keywords**: \"react testing\" is better than just \"testing\"\n2. **Try alternative terms**: If \"deploy\" doesn't work, try \"deployment\" or \"ci-cd\"\n3. **Check popular sources**: Many skills come from `vercel-labs/agent-skills` or `ComposioHQ/awesome-claude-skills`\n\n## When No Skills Are Found\n\nIf no relevant skills exist:\n\n1. Acknowledge that no existing skill was found\n2. Offer to help with the task directly using your general capabilities\n3. Suggest the user could create their own skill with `npx skills init`\n\nExample:\n\n```\nI searched for skills related to \"xyz\" but didn't find any matches.\nI can still help you with this task directly! Would you like me to proceed?\n\nIf this is something you do often, you could create your own skill:\nnpx skills init my-xyz-skill\n```\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1773498682854}}
{"type":"message","id":"c68f4308","parentId":"3ddec455","timestamp":"2026-03-14T14:31:38.142Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"**Explaining skill execution**\n\nI need to clarify how the skill executes based on operator policy. The user is asking how Skill runs, so I want to explain that the original skill involves using “npx skills,” but the current operator policy overrides this method. Instead, it requires using Skillhub first. This is crucial information to provide for understanding how the execution process has changed.","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_06eb29bac2029a2b0169b5713d5be4819184615f1126309539\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"encrypted_content\":\"gAAAAABptXFBdMULm238FJY99Fxd0qO64smaXkNQVpnnhoKoJeAfAaLa4fr44EsgYhAgjD8LJybvgyVjbsciLeBfbNEBnsfG3dMpAXYv3GRJe5w08JQ86tJlH_B3MBFqQGg1ZfQgwsRRL7X0YgfglrFX4osChOJBQELyLgs1qw4G58vnarUbroIYP0_AbWUxmOfj4kGcG2FgX6ddyGEodLw0SjE9rcSQ61PYK7QFASzjFHUn6DTjeLvfHN_TPiPoapIVd2rkW44SqonWWz8eqw1W12ap6pqdcHuHrew4vbC2gJGIoai3M2qZHBjR-Aawxn7dowiacJ0VzniC5RnJK_Y8FYj5RD6bacUlJkgha5k0IL0p_6ZLQMPDylpF_8T-bF5POJucUgDHwojopz8_eVJahFRpxvMzkI_GKuqeX1kkLz13er2ZLUZ_wDUfI3E4fUwrVGv7GSl3eM756lulBKqxXSnv1pHe7Wc4yKvBjVMO_lg4cLHKcmKdcJ1z_mUZ9TM1nLC8XPZmoBez93x5hnX7-lHMbGn0cwD7sQVLKp0RC0_FZaR64zMhL_NcPXYOi-XHt_algw0NBGn1J-yxLoKUN63gM3P_gtomv6QJZ0Lv6Rievbd3e-ZCbV0996K9lcBlWsFWl41rdv5rsJBZYcvb8a10lFGdhQkSY1HLsFe8wEPLOs-mBJ4k8K8Cp-gNWwc44w4l2oJiI8-yPomEu6yVbdur4YY5d6f0hYGcs3ZnteE3XZa1iE_p6bWqD7JHyC-o5JdK_MtSTURhb8WVZNgAEWyr2LwE8ruTqe9T8LmuelcNJ_5GivYcYWfdtOj9YNRuJq7buse74v7n4tYUtRUlHQlzQjhTGxPdowdLhT8atfIOom5vpT_n1ZmxtY1WvzruhAW0Eghoez4HsBI0JNSmAcEkX6z8b3RIHqw38DZnM-Wc90OhECpZKXOQlOnC-IDJsmKHMekTbKqqFu5c5gxVceYnBvz-mentTbdz17LFCTgRJNW_DKTnY6RxfgiMUuBRa9W-mwVifddPWHn44TJDhPEYPxzZXMhAvOZMtZuB3ln7k1bVNAemP2gTCavPoLSaILu36xqqa0HeiiNrheuHZlahN89PoQ==\",\"summary\":[{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Explaining skill execution**\\n\\nI need to clarify how the skill executes based on operator policy. The user is asking how Skill runs, so I want to explain that the original skill involves using “npx skills,” but the current operator policy overrides this method. Instead, it requires using Skillhub first. This is crucial information to provide for understanding how the execution process has changed.\"}]}"},{"type":"text","text":"[[reply_to_current]] 这个 **find-skills** 的执行逻辑，核心就是：**当你在问“有没有现成技能能做某件事”时，先帮你搜技能，再把结果整理给你，必要时再安装。**\n\n### 它原始设计是怎么跑的\n这个 skill 的 `SKILL.md` 里定义的是：\n\n1. **识别需求**\n   - 先判断你想扩展什么能力\n   - 比如 React、测试、部署、文档、GitHub、设计这些方向\n\n2. **搜索技能**\n   - 原始写法是用：\n   ```bash\n   npx skills find <query>\n   ```\n   - 比如你说“找个 PR review 的 skill”，它就会搜类似 `pr review`\n\n3. **展示结果**\n   - 告诉你找到什么 skill\n   - 给出安装命令\n   - 给出详情链接\n\n4. **如果你同意，再安装**\n   - 原始写法是：\n   ```bash\n   npx skills add <owner/repo@skill> -g -y\n   ```\n\n---\n\n### 但你这边现在实际不是完全按它原文跑\n因为你这台 OpenClaw 现在有更高优先级的 **operator policy**，所以执行时要按你现在这套规则来：\n\n#### 搜索时\n**先走 `skillhub`**\n而且必须先执行：\n```bash\nskillhub search <关键词>\n```\n\n如果：\n- `skillhub` 不可用\n- 被限流\n- 没结果\n\n再 fallback 到 **`clawhub`**。\n\n#### 安装前\n不能直接装，必须先告诉你：\n- 来源\n- 版本\n- 风险信号\n\n然后再装。\n\n---\n\n### 所以现在这个 skill 的“实际运行方式”可以理解成\n不是死板照着 `SKILL.md` 里的 `npx skills` 执行，  \n而是：\n\n1. **find-skills 负责判断“该不该找 skill、搜什么关键词”**\n2. **真正搜索/安装时，遵守你当前机器的 operator policy**\n   - 搜索优先 `skillhub`\n   - 不行再 `clawhub`\n   - 安装前先汇报来源、版本、风险\n\n---\n\n### 一句话总结\n**find-skills 是“找技能的决策流程”，不是你这台机器上的最终底层包管理规范。**  \n在你这里，它会被当前策略接管成：\n\n- **搜索**：`skillhub search <keywords>`\n- **回退**：`clawhub`\n- **安装前**：先做来源/版本/风险说明\n\n如果你要，我下一步可以直接给你演示一次：  \n比如你随便说个需求，我按现在这套真实规则跑一遍给你看。","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_06eb29bac2029a2b0169b571411a6c8191984ac94589123644\",\"phase\":\"final_answer\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":1264,"output":669,"cacheRead":159232,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":161165,"cost":{"input":0.00316,"output":0.010035,"cacheRead":0.039807999999999996,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.053002999999999995}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1773498682861}}
{"type":"message","id":"c70faf72","parentId":"c68f4308","timestamp":"2026-03-14T14:33:56.634Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Skills store policy (operator configured):\n1. For skills discovery/install/update, try `skillhub` first (cn-optimized).\n2. If unavailable, rate-limited, or no match, fallback to `clawhub` (public-registry).\n3. Do not claim exclusivity. Public and private registries are both allowed.\n4. Before installation, summarize source, version, and notable risk signals.\n5. For search requests, execute `exec` with `skillhub search <keywords>` first and report the command output.\n6. In the current session, reply directly. Do NOT call `message` tool just to send progress updates.\n\nConversation info (untrusted metadata):\n```json\n{\n  \"message_id\": \"om_x100b546353f318a4b10a791e3202e44\",\n  \"sender_id\": \"ou_5abeeb52afc248214694d8d79ab20df8\",\n  \"sender\": \"范\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"Sat 2026-03-14 22:33 GMT+8\"\n}\n```\n\nSender (untrusted metadata):\n```json\n{\n  \"label\": \"范 (ou_5abeeb52afc248214694d8d79ab20df8)\",\n  \"id\": \"ou_5abeeb52afc248214694d8d79ab20df8\",\n  \"name\": \"范\"\n}\n```\n\n[message_id: om_x100b546353f318a4b10a791e3202e44]\n范: 我想修改这套 operator policy 的流程：不去skillhub搜索，直接去clawhub搜索 skills"}],"timestamp":1773498836619}}
